00:02:00.789 --> 00:02:03.509
But in all seriousness, let's not write it
off.

00:02:03.509 --> 00:02:09.950
And what I mean by that is remember that Trump
won the Republican primary of 2016.

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:12.720
Trump then won the presidential election.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:18.250
You could come to me with tears in your eyes
and say, Sir, Trump is considering Jeffrey

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:21.330
Dahmer where he's still alive as VP.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:25.890
And I'd say, That's insane, and he still might
win.

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:30.690
The most depressing era in a long time, for
sure.

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:36.180
And I don't think GREENE necessarily hurts
Trump.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:40.460
Now, on the other hand, I don't know that
she necessarily helps.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:46.959
And what I mean by that is, like, in all seriousness,
does Marjorie Taylor GREENE bring any new

00:02:46.959 --> 00:02:49.540
voters to Donald Trump?

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:51.150
I don't know that she does.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:58.890
If you are in the Romney wing of the Republican
Party or the Liz Cheney wing of the Republican

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:04.850
Party, and you don't like Democrats, but you're
just not sold on Trump.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:09.470
If Trump picks Romney, maybe you go with the
Trump Romney ticket.

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:10.709
Now, that's not being considered.

00:03:10.709 --> 00:03:15.680
I'm just saying maybe that gets you to go
